  "label": "Autism Awareness Month is being 'taken' by 'her'",
  "description": "The text overlay 'when she finally has your own month' is mapped onto the visual entity 'autism_bead_display'. The visual material (the beads spelling 'AUTISM') represents Autism Awareness Month, and the text implies that 'she' (a woman) is claiming or 'taking' this month, which is framed as a sarcastic or mocking commentary. This mapping projects the textual concept of 'her taking your month' onto the visual representation of 'AUTISM' beads, creating an analogical relationship where the beads symbolize the month being 'taken'.",
